~ prologue_edict

Unknown: A family in the ossuary, watching a clerk scrape their father's name off his niche. [ID:JOURNAL_PROLOGUE_EDICT]

=> END

~ prologue_singer

Unknown: The choir in gold, and the dove singing a list of names, and a hole in the light by the door. [ID:JOURNAL_PROLOGUE_SINGER]

=> END

~ greybox_altar

Unknown: The chapel before the fire, and one word carved into its altar: Mercy. [ID:JOURNAL_GREYBOX_ALTAR]

=> END

~ greybox_milestone

Unknown: The road beyond the gate, warm and busy, as if it still went somewhere. [ID:JOURNAL_GREYBOX_MILESTONE]

=> END
